# Dev loop

Cloud writes verbs and research. This PC is PixelLab and Play. Do not move that split.

## Next-action line

The first local reply, and the last reply of a cloud or sign-off turn, is one short line. Use these words. Do not invent a paragraph of git advice.

- One open PR, tree clean, checks green or unknown, not an art/ideas chat: Ready for Play. Open the `game` folder in Godot and press Play. When it feels right, say done.
- PR still building / checks red: Not ready for Play yet. Wait until the PR is green, then start this chat again — or say playtest and I will check.
- Several open PRs: Which PR are we playtesting?
- Dirty tree: This PC has unsaved work. Say save so GitHub matches before we switch branches.
- On main, clean, no PR: GitHub matches this PC. Say top 3 for the next slice, or PixelLab for art.
- After plan (verbs/research): Click Build in Cloud. Do not playtest there. When the PR is up, start a new local chat — I will tell you when Godot is ready.
- Cloud PR opened: PR is up. Start a new local chat on the Surface for Play. I will not open Godot here.
- After `done` / `good` / `save`: main matches GitHub. Start a new chat for the next idea.
- Play found a small problem: Say what felt wrong. I will patch this branch. Then press Play again.

## Cloud

- Open a PR. Run headless tests and wait for Actions. You may claim REVIEW gates 1–5.
- Never launch the Godot editor. Never claim Play. Gate 6 is the owner on this PC.
- STATUS says **ready for Play**, not signed off.
- End with the Cloud PR opened line.

## Local

- Session start injects branch, dirty tree, and open PRs. Follow `.cursor/skills/playtest-pr`.
- Exactly one open PR, tree clean, not an art / PixelLab / `top 3` chat: land it, then the Ready for Play line.
- `playtest` always lands when the tree is clean and the PR is known.
- Do not open Godot. The owner presses Play.
- Small Play notes stay in this chat. Patch the PR branch. Do not start a third agent.

## Sign-off

Sign-off words mean GitHub `main` matches this PC. On a PR branch that includes merge, checkout `main`, and pull. Detail: `.cursor/rules/commit-signoff.mdc` and the Sync job in `.cursor/skills/playtest-pr`.
